    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1294">

                <pb facs="1097" n="993" xml:id="pg993"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.1216M/421.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-05-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 3, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>220. The Department’s telegram of May 2 re Colorado River. Minister of Fomento
                    states he is in practical agreement with the Department’s counter-draft of the
                    amended convention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—On May 8, 1913, the Ambassador
                        included in a telegram<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1294-f1"/> covering various
                        subjects brought up in an interview with General Huerta the information that
                        Huerta had refused to consider the Colorado River question until formal
                        recognition of his administration by the United States. No further action
                        appears to have been taken during 1913.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1294-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1294-f1-content">
